2. Business records stored on your device

Werkm8 is offline-first. Customer and job records, quotes, invoices, time tracking, materials, measurements, appointments, reminders, notes, templates, photos, receipts, signatures and financial summaries are generally stored locally on your device. The developer does not require you to store those records in a developer-operated business cloud.

You control what you enter, export, share, back up or synchronize. As a self-employed tradesperson handling your own customers' personal data, you will generally be responsible for your lawful customer-data processing under the GDPR.

Offline-first does not mean that the app never communicates over the internet. Authentication, licensing, security protection and optionally enabled online features are explained below.

3. Google sign-in, trials and licensing

Werkm8 uses Google sign-in via Firebase Authentication. Firebase and Google Cloud services issue, verify and restore trial or paid licences and manage permitted devices.

For these purposes the following data may be processed: Firebase user identifier (UID), Google account details made available on sign-in (including email address and display name), trial and licence status, timestamps, purchase and entitlement information, a pseudonymous hashed device identifier, and limited device model/name information. Account and licence information is processed online; the local business database is not routinely uploaded for licence verification.

Google Play handles purchases and payments. Werkm8 uses purchase and entitlement status to activate and recover licences. The developer does not need your full payment-card details for licence verification.

The legal basis for account and licence processing is GDPR Article 6(1)(b) (performance of the service). Security and anti-abuse measures rely on legitimate interests under Article 6(1)(f). Initial sign-in and occasional licence verification require internet access; many business functions can work offline with a valid offline entitlement.

4. Security and crash diagnostics

Werkm8 integrates Firebase App Check and Google Play Integrity to protect connected services. Google may process technical app and device attestation data.

Firebase Crashlytics is integrated for technical error diagnosis. Reports may include installation/session identifiers, device model, operating system and app versions, timestamps, stack traces, error reports and messages. Such diagnostics are not necessarily anonymous and are not intended as a storage system for customer or job records.

The legal basis is GDPR Article 6(1)(f) (security and reliable operation). According to Firebase, Crashlytics retains crash data and related identifiers for 90 days before starting deletion: https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy

5. Optional encrypted backups and Dropbox sync

Werkm8 offers local backups and password-encrypted exports. Where available in the installed version and chosen by the user, Werkm8 may also offer encrypted backups or synchronization of selected business records and attachments through the user's Dropbox account.

Depending on the selected categories, the encrypted uploads may include customer and job data, documents, appointments, photos or receipts. Encryption occurs on the device before upload. Keep the encryption password safe. Dropbox also processes its own account, authorization and connection metadata according to its privacy policy. The Android app may store reconnect credentials in Android-protected app storage.

The optional backup/synchronization is provided on the user's request under GDPR Article 6(1)(b). Disconnecting Dropbox does not automatically delete previously uploaded files; you manage these in Dropbox.

Dropbox privacy: https://www.dropbox.com/privacy

6. Device permissions, maps and sharing

Depending on features used, the app may request camera/scanner access (photos and receipts), files (PDFs, documents and backups), and notifications (appointments/reminders). Using these permissions does not automatically upload local business records.

Opening or embedding Google Maps can share address details and connection data with Google. When you share PDFs, photos or emails using another app, the chosen provider handles the information you provide under its own terms.

7. Providers, international processing and security

Relevant providers include Google (Google sign-in, Firebase Authentication, Firebase/Google Cloud backend, Google Play, App Check, Play Integrity and Crashlytics) and, only if you use it, Dropbox. Maps and expressly selected sharing services may also receive data.

Depending on the service, data may be processed outside the European Economic Area. Google states that Firebase Authentication is processed in US data centres. Where required, applicable international-transfer mechanisms and provider safeguards apply.

Provider information:
https://policies.google.com/privacy
https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy
https://www.dropbox.com/privacy

Werkm8 does not sell your business records to advertisers.

8. Retention, account deletion and requests

Local customer and business records remain on your device until removed or the app's data is deleted. Copies exported or saved via other apps or Dropbox must be managed separately.

Online account, licence, purchase-verification and security records are kept only as needed for their purposes, misuse prevention, support, existing entitlements or applicable legal duties. Uninstalling the app does not automatically delete these records. Firebase states that after an authentication user deletion is initiated, related data is removed from live and backup systems within 180 days; other data is subject to its own deletion processes and necessary retention rules.

To request deletion of your Werkm8 account and personal information controlled by the developer, email wanderschreiner@googlemail.com. You can do this without having the app installed. Identity verification may be necessary. Some records may be retained where legally required. Deleting Werkm8 does not delete your Google or Dropbox account.

9. GDPR rights

Subject to applicable law, you may have rights of access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability and objection to processing based on legitimate interests. You may also complain to a competent data-protection supervisory authority. Direct requests regarding developer-controlled information to the privacy contact above.

10. Intended users and changes

Werkm8 is for professional use by tradespeople, not children. This notice may be updated when features, providers or applicable law change.
